# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  .easignore — what is EXCLUDED FROM THE EAS BUILD UPLOAD.
#
#  Nothing here is deleted: every path stays on disk and in git. This file only
#  keeps ~880 MB of QA evidence and tooling out of the archive shipped to the
#  build worker. Uploading it caused the "Bundle JavaScript" phase to fail with
#  an unknown error on every production build attempt (2026-06-06, 06-07 and
#  08-20 / 4e3ef541); the same bundle succeeds locally with identical
#  production env, which is what pointed at the archive rather than the code.
#
#  DELIBERATE EXCEPTION: app/mldiag.tsx require()s the bundled TFLite test
#  images, so qa-artifacts/tflite-test-set/bundled MUST stay in the upload or
#  the bundle cannot resolve those modules.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# QA evidence — keep only the bundled test set the app actually imports.
qa-artifacts/*
!qa-artifacts/tflite-test-set
qa-artifacts/tflite-test-set/*
!qa-artifacts/tflite-test-set/bundled

# ── Mirror of .gitignore ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  A .easignore REPLACES .gitignore for the upload, so everything .gitignore
#  used to keep out must be repeated here. Critically that includes the
#  generated native projects: android/ and ios/ are produced by prebuild, and
#  uploading them flips EAS from the managed workflow into the BARE workflow,
#  where the app config's runtimeVersion policy is unsupported and the build
#  aborts before it starts.
node_modules/
.expo/
web-build/
.next/
out/
.turbo/
coverage/
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
supabase/.temp/
.DS_Store
android/
ios/
**/xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
.vercel
*.pem
*.key
*.p8
*.p12
*.tsbuildinfo

# Knowledge graph, local build trees and release artifacts.
graphify-out
dist
dist-*
*.apk
*.aab
*.ipa

# Local logs and scratch output.
*.log
